course: dictionary
lesson: 15874
title: Things nobody knows yet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that something is not known yet. Unidentified means not known or not recognised: nobody has worked out yet who or what it is. The prefix un- means not, and identified means named or recognised, so unidentified means not yet named.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The police asked people to help find an unidentified man.» The word man tells you it is a person, and the police want help because his name is still a mystery. Try your meaning in the sentence: "find a man whose name is not known" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Scientists and storytellers use this word too. «Scientists found an unidentified sea creature.» They have seen it, but they have not named or explained it yet. In a story, «Something unidentified moved in the dark woods» makes the reader feel curious and a little scared.
fact: Unidentified means not known or not recognised.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unidentified means not yet identified.
fact: «An unidentified flying object» is often shortened to UFO.
fact: «An unidentified person» is someone whose name is not known.
fact: Scientists use the word for unidentified species, which are waiting to be named.
exercise: «The police asked for help to find an unidentified man.» What does unidentified mean here? | Who has been found and named | Who is very tall | *Whose name is not known | Who is lost at sea
exercise: What does the short form UFO stand for? | Unusual field of owls | Upside-down flying oven | Unknown fast orange | *Unidentified flying object
exercise: «The scientists studied the unidentified creature for weeks.» Find and copy the word that means not known yet. | studied | creature | weeks | *unidentified
test: «Mum said the thing in the sky was an unidentified flying object.» Why is it called unidentified? | It is too small to see | *Nobody can explain or name it yet | It belongs to a pilot | It is painted gold
test: «The lost bag had no name on it, so the owner stayed unidentified.» What does stayed unidentified suggest? | *The owner was still not known | The owner was happy to be found | The owner was a famous singer | The owner had gone home
exam: «The unidentified species was found in the deep sea, and no one knew its name.» What does this sentence suggest about the species? | It was a common fish from the shop | It was already famous | *Its name and nature were not yet known | It was made by people
